    {
      "id": "name",
      "text": "His name was Garrett Morgan, a Black inventor in Cleveland.",
      "visual": {
        "kind": "card",
        "image": "portrait",
        "crop": [
          0.0,
          0.0,
          1.0,
          1.0
        ],
        "caption": "Garrett A. Morgan"
      },
      "section": "who",
      "overlays": {
        "lowerThird": {
          "name": "Garrett Morgan",
          "sub": "Inventor · 1877 – 1963"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "blast",
      "text": "In July 1916, a tunnel being dug under Lake Erie exploded, and gas filled it.",
      "visual": {
        "kind": "title",
        "title": "July 1916",
        "sub": "an explosion under Lake Erie"
      },
      "section": "story",
      "overlays": {
        "pin": {
          "label": "Cleveland",
          "sub": "Ohio"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "trapped",
      "text": "Men were trapped inside. Rescuers went in, and the gas killed them too.",
      "visual": {
        "kind": "card",
        "image": "rescue",
        "crop": [
          0.05,
          0.05,
          0.95,
          0.55
        ],
        "caption": "The crowd at the tunnel, July 1916"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "call",
      "text": "So the police called Morgan.",
      "visual": {
        "kind": "card",
        "image": "portrait",
        "crop": [
          0.12,
          0.08,
          0.88,
          0.8
        ],
        "caption": "Garrett A. Morgan"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "patent",
      "text": "Two years earlier, he had patented a breathing hood.",
      "visual": {
        "kind": "card",
        "image": "hood1",
        "crop": [
          0.12,
          0.04,
          0.86,
          0.72
        ],
        "caption": "US Patent 1,113,675, 1914",
        "clipping": true
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "down",
      "text": "He and his brother Frank put on the hoods and went down into the gas.",
      "visual": {
        "kind": "card",
        "image": "hood1",
        "crop": [
          0.13,
          0.17,
          0.42,
          0.72
        ],
        "caption": "The hood and its air tube, patent drawing, 1914"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "survivors",
      "text": "They came back up carrying survivors.",
      "visual": {
        "kind": "card",
        "image": "rescue",
        "crop": [
          0.0,
          0.0,
          1.0,
          1.0
        ],
        "caption": "Cleveland newspaper, July 1916",
        "clipping": true
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "denied",
      "text": "But he was denied the credit and the reward the other rescuers got.",
      "visual": {
        "kind": "title",
        "title": "No reward",
        "sub": "and his name left out of the news"
      },
      "section": "cost"
    },
    {
      "id": "racism",
      "text": "Racism had already hurt his business. To sell his hood, he hired a white man to act as the salesman.",
      "visual": {
        "kind": "card",
        "image": "hood2",
        "crop": [
          0.1,
          0.05,
          0.9,
          0.75
        ],
        "caption": "US Patent 1,113,675, sheet 2"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "crash",
      "text": "Later, after seeing a crash at an intersection, he patented a new traffic signal.",
      "visual": {
        "kind": "card",
        "image": "signal",
        "crop": [
          0.0,
          0.0,
          1.0,
          0.75
        ],
        "caption": "US Patent 1,475,024, 1923",
        "clipping": true
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "ge",
      "text": "General Electric bought it for 40,000 dollars.",
      "visual": {
        "kind": "title",
        "title": "$40,000",
        "sub": "paid by General Electric"
      },
      "overlays": {
        "stamp": "Sold"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "legacy",
      "text": "He walked into the dark so others could walk out.",
      "visual": {
